# Earthling Aidtech — marketing site (Astro, static, GitHub Pages)
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERYTHING IN THIS FILE IS PUBLIC. THAT IS THE POINT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This site builds to static HTML/JS. Astro only exposes variables prefixed
# with `PUBLIC_` to that bundle, and it does so by *inlining the literal value*
# into the shipped JavaScript. There is no server to keep anything back.
#
# So: a `PUBLIC_` variable is not "configuration" — it is text you are printing
# on the homepage. Never put an API key, SMTP password, database URL, admin
# password or signing secret behind the `PUBLIC_` prefix, in this repo or in
# the GitHub Actions environment that builds it. Server-side secrets belong to
# the API project (backend/, deployed on Vercel) and live in Vercel's
# Environment Variables, never here.

# Origin of the lead-capture API — the separate Vercel project that owns
# POST /api/leads and the admin dashboard. Public by design: it is just the
# hostname the browser is about to connect to, visible in devtools on the
# first submit anyway. The API is what enforces CORS, rate limits and auth.
#
# Leave unset in production: the site falls back to the value below.
# Set it to point a local build at a local API (`vercel dev` in backend/).
PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.earthlingaidtech.com
